<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Merged into the bundled app's Info.plist by the Tauri bundler, and embedded
  into the binary by tauri-codegen for `tauri dev`. Without the microphone
  usage string macOS kills the process the moment cpal opens an input device,
  in dev and in the bundle alike.

  Accessibility (needed for the synthetic Cmd+V paste) has no Info.plist key.
  It is granted at runtime in System Settings; paste.rs checks AXIsProcessTrusted().

  LSUIElement is deliberately NOT set here: hiding the Dock icon is a product
  decision (it also stops the app stealing focus from the app being dictated
  into), not a packaging one. See the rehaul notes before turning it on.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Inkwell records audio only while you hold the dictation shortcut. Speech is transcribed on this Mac and the recording never leaves it.</string>
	<key>NSHighResolutionCapable</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
